2. Font art — CC BY 4.0
-----------------------

The glyph art and everything built from it: `glyphs/`, `fonts/*.mcm`,
`assets/logo_288x72.png`, and `previews/`.

SPDX-License-Identifier: CC-BY-4.0

Copyright (c) 2026 Army Jay

Licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License.
Full text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

In short: you may share and adapt this font, including commercially, so
long as you give appropriate credit. Attribution 4.0 was chosen over a
share-alike licence deliberately — a pilot who wants to swap one glyph for
their own should not inherit a copyleft obligation on the rest of their
config.

Suggested attribution:

    Army Jay OSD font — https://github.com/chalkyjason/edgesounds
    Licensed CC BY 4.0


3. Third-party — not ours to license
------------------------------------

`assets/references/stock/default_v1.mcm`
`assets/references/stock/default_v2.mcm`
`assets/references/png/*`

These are the stock Betaflight analog OSD fonts, taken unmodified from
betaflight/betaflight-configurator (`resources/osd/1/default.mcm` and
`resources/osd/2/default.mcm`, commit 505bd6d), and the PNGs are a
mechanical decode of the second. They are Copyright the Betaflight project
and its contributors, licensed **GPL-3.0**, and are included here solely as
a shape reference and as a test fixture for round-trip verification.

  Betaflight Configurator: https://github.com/betaflight/betaflight-configurator
  GPL-3.0: https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.txt

No stock glyph art is used as a build base. The only bytes that reach a
built font from stock are the two protected indexes, `0x00` and `0xFF`,
both of which are blank.

`tools/crosscheck_configurator.mjs` executes Configurator source from a
checkout you supply. It does not copy or redistribute any of that source.


A note on the licensing choice
------------------------------

These terms were selected as sensible defaults for an FPV community font,
not on legal advice. They are the author's to change: edit this file and
the licence section in README.md. If you would rather the art were
CC BY-SA, CC0, or the SIL Open Font License, nothing in the build depends
on this choice.
